<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><title>Cancellation & Withdrawal | Matrix Reprogrammed</title><meta name="description" content="How to cancel a Matrix Reprogrammed membership and exercise applicable consumer withdrawal rights."><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="fixes.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="reader-experience.css"></head>
<body><canvas id="matrix"></canvas><div class="page"><header class="wrap topbar"><a class="brand" href="index.html">MATRIX REPROGRAMMED</a><nav class="nav"><a href="membership.html">Membership</a><a href="billing-dashboard.html">Billing</a><a href="membership-terms.html">Terms</a><a href="legal-notice.html">Legal Notice</a></nav></header><main class="wrap section"><div class="eyebrow">Version 2026-07-18-v1</div><h1>CANCELLATION &amp; WITHDRAWAL.</h1><p class="lead">This notice separates ordinary subscription cancellation from any statutory right to withdraw from a distance contract.</p>
<section class="section"><h2>Cancel future renewals</h2><p>You can request cancellation from the Matrix Reprogrammed billing dashboard or through your PayPal account. The cancellation request is sent to PayPal and recorded in the Matrix Reprogrammed billing ledger. Where PayPal confirms a paid period remains, member access may continue until that period ends. Future monthly renewals stop after PayPal processes the cancellation.</p><p><a class="btn" href="billing-dashboard.html">Open Billing Dashboard</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Withdrawal request</h2><p>Where mandatory consumer law gives you a withdrawal period for a distance contract, you may send an unambiguous withdrawal request to <a href="mailto:members@matrixreprogrammed.com">members@matrixreprogrammed.com</a>. Include the account email, selected membership tier, PayPal subscription or transaction reference if available, and a clear statement that you wish to withdraw.</p><p>You may use this wording: “I hereby give notice that I withdraw from my contract for the following Matrix Reprogrammed membership: [tier], ordered on [date], account email [email].” A specific form is not required where the law accepts any clear statement.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Immediate digital service</h2><p>Paid member services are designed to begin immediately after PayPal confirms an active subscription. Before checkout opens, the member must expressly request immediate performance and acknowledge this notice. Statutory withdrawal rights remain unless and only to the extent that a valid legal exception applies. A checkbox alone is not treated as permission to ignore mandatory consumer rights.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Refunds, reversals and billing disputes</h2><p>A cancellation is not automatically a refund. Refund and reversal requests are assessed against the verified PayPal transaction, applicable law and the circumstances of the request. A verified refund or reversal places the related paid entitlement on hold or removes it. PayPal may also provide its own dispute process.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Processing and confirmation</h2><p>Support will use the verified account and PayPal records to identify the subscription. Do not send passwords, complete card numbers or PayPal credentials. A cancellation or withdrawal response will be sent through the verified account email where possible.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Consumer rights</h2><p>Nothing on this page excludes rights that cannot legally be excluded. Before live checkout is enabled, the Legal Notice must display the verified commercial operator details, governing consumer information and applicable mediation route.</p></section>
